                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Painkiller: Overdose: More of the Same, With Less of the Fun[/h1]\r\n\r\n[b]Gameplay & Gunplay: 7/10[/b]\r\n\r\n[i]The shooting itself isn't the problem. If you've played Painkiller, you know what you're getting: fast, simple and familiar. But there's nothing new here, and you're just doing the same thing again.[/i]\r\n\r\n[b]Level Design & Structure: 4.5/10[/b]\r\n\r\n[i]This is where the game falls apart. The levels and their structure are extremely repetitive and boring, and no matter how hard I tried to push through, I couldn't get much further. It was the level design and nothing else that made me drop it, not the graphics and not the gameplay.[/i]\r\n\r\n[b]Graphics & Sound: 7/10[/b]\r\n\r\n[i]Nothing here bothered me. The visuals and sound do the job and fit the genre, but nothing stands out either.[/i]\r\n\r\n[b]Innovation & Content: 5/10[/b]\r\n\r\n[i]There's no innovation at all. It feels like it was released just to be released, with no special points to make it memorable.[/i]\r\n\r\n[b]Value: 6.5/10[/b]\r\n\r\n[i]It might be fine for someone who's sick in bed with nothing better to do. But if you're looking for an experience and real enjoyment, you won't get much out of it.[/i]\r\n\r\n[h1]Final Thoughts[/h1]\r\n\r\n[i]Painkiller: Overdose is weak, repetitive and lacks any new ideas. The gameplay is okay and the presentation is fine, but the level design is so tiresome that I dropped it quickly and couldn't make myself go back. I'd only recommend buying it if you're a huge Painkiller fan. Otherwise, it isn't worth your money or your time.[/i]\r\n\r\n[h1]Final Score: 6/10[/h1]\r\n\r\n[b]Verdict: Not Recommended[/b]\r\n\r\n[i]A repetitive, uninspired expansion that only die-hard Painkiller fans should consider.[/i]",
